        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Painting a ceiling well comes down to prep and rhythm. Empty and cover the room, wash and patch the surface, prime what needs it, then cut in and roll one section at a time while every edge is still wet. Two moderate coats beat one heavy one almost every time.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Pick a paint made for ceilings, a 3/8-inch roller for smooth drywall and an extension pole, and the job gets far easier. Our <a href="/best-ceiling-paint/">ceiling paint picks</a> cover the low-spatter, flat and stain-blocking options worth buying.
          </p>
